<$link to="a quoted attribute value with no closing quote anywhere ahead

A WIDGET'S QUOTED ATTRIBUTE VALUE CARRIES ACROSS A BLANK LINE. TiddlyWiki refuses the whole tag where
no closing quote stands anywhere in the source, and builds the element across the break where one
does — of eleven accepted start tags carrying a blank line, eight carry it inside a quoted value. So
the string region carries on, and a cut landing inside one leaves the widget's own region standing.

This carrier stands alone because an open quote consumes the rest of its source.
